  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ELEVATE ; Enhanced Resilience via Integrated Approach and Digital Technology</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">An integrated Governance Approach is crucial to enhance public service delivery and optimize resource use across sectors. this approach brings together different levels of government, ministries, local authorities, and civil society to coordinate policies and strategies that are responsive to the diverse needs of Indonesias population. The Water-Energy-Food (WEF) Nexus offers a model for integrated resource management that acknowledges the interconnections between these crucial sectors. By fostering collaboration and breaking down silos in decision-making, this framework can help address disparities between regions and social groups, providing a foundation for inclusive development. It is evident that achieving integrated governance, enhanced service delivery and participatory planning are considered achievable by leveraging innovation and digital technology. By combining the WEF framework and digital innovation, Indonesia can improve public service delivery, enhance resources management and ensure that development benefits all citizens.</narrative>
  </description>
